119
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.480
Because we always say there wasn't a true Thanksgiving episode of The Office.

120
00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:27.720
Yeah, I have been holding on to this for so long.

121
00:05:27.720 --> 00:05:30.480
I found an old file with a bunch of story pitches.

122
00:05:30.820 --> 00:05:35.260
And there was one in the season three file called Thanksgiving.

123
00:05:36.140 --> 00:05:37.220
It's pretty wild.

124
00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:40.480
Now, just remember, this is just a pitch document.

125
00:05:40.480 --> 00:05:45.300
It was never written, but it gives you a glimpse at what our writers would put together.

126
00:05:45.300 --> 00:05:46.340
I can't wait.

127
00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:47.300
Are you going to read it to us?

128
00:05:47.380 --> 00:05:47.620
Yes.

129
00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:47.880
Okay.

130
00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:48.680
Here it is.

131
00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:51.260
It is Wednesday of Thanksgiving week.

132
00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:55.940
We start in the kitchen where Angela enters and no one will talk to her.

133
00:05:56.180 --> 00:06:03.760
In a talking head, Phyllis mentions that Angela is suing the company for $8.6 million because of Oscar's slap.

134
00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:15.540
So, I guess during season three, before this episode, there was a pitch that for some reason I could not figure out why Oscar was going to have slapped Angela.

135
00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.740
She was probably being a real bitch and he had had it.

136
00:06:18.920 --> 00:06:19.200
All right.

137
00:06:19.240 --> 00:06:22.820
So, now we find out that Michael has chosen to ignore this lawsuit.

138
00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:25.760
It doesn't name him personally, so it's not his problem.

139
00:06:26.020 --> 00:06:29.940
He is also excited because he's going to spend Thanksgiving with Carol.

140
00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:34.880
Dwight is nervous because the shrewd Thanksgiving is going to be at Shrewd Farms this year.

141
00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:39.720
And moreover, he has decided to have his girlfriend meet his family.

142
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:45.920
His girlfriend being Angela, although he doesn't tell everyone in the office who he means.

143
00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:50.380
Well, Michael hears about the shrewd gathering and the document says he shits on it.

144
00:06:51.300 --> 00:06:54.740
Michael says, a hundred shrewds in one barn?

145
00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:55.940
Dork convention.

146
00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.280
So, now Carol comes to see Michael at the office.

147
00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:04.000
She says, this is hard, but I think my kids should be with their father on Thanksgiving.

148
00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.680
So, we're driving to Maryland.

149
00:07:06.740 --> 00:07:09.000
Michael says, that's going to be awkward.

150
00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.260
Is Rick going to be okay with me being there?

151
00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:12.900
Carol says, no.

152
00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.900
That's why you're not coming.

153
00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:21.900
Then, in a talking head, Carol reveals that she's been reconciling with her ex and is essentially calling it off by going there.

154
00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:26.960
Though, Michael doesn't necessarily realize the long-term implications of her actions.

155
00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:31.140
So, now, Michael is sad because he has no place to go.

156
00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:38.720
Dwight's brother, a doctor from Seattle, and then in parentheses it says, who will be played by Paul Feig.

157
00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:39.320
Oh.

158
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:40.080
Mm-hmm.

159
00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.660
Comes in to the office to visit Dwight.

160
00:07:43.040 --> 00:07:46.580
Dwight introduces him to Michael, and he kind of hits it off with Michael,

161
00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:53.080
and he invites him to the shrewd pre-Thanksgiving dinner that night because Thanksgiving is shrewds only.

162
00:07:53.540 --> 00:07:54.260
Michael considers.

163
00:07:54.640 --> 00:07:59.360
But Dwight is nervous about Michael coming because Angela is coming over and there's still a secret.

164
00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:03.840
Wait, does Dwight have to choose between Angela and Michael?

165
00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:05.540
Yes, at firSt.

166
00:08:05.780 --> 00:08:07.800
Because Dwight says to Angela, can Michael just be there?

167
00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.960
And Angela says, I don't think it's a good idea because then Michael will know about us and it might hurt my lawsuit.

168
00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.400
So, Dwight is very conflicted.

169
00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:21.560
But eventually, he feels like, well, my brother Paul invited Michael and I'm going to honor that.

170
00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.480
And he's also really excited for Michael to meet his dad.

171
00:08:25.020 --> 00:08:27.220
So, Michael heads to Dwight's farm.

172
00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:30.200
He is confused when he sees Angela there.

173
00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:37.420
And Dwight awkwardly covers and says, oh, my girlfriend couldn't make it because she had to go to Kuwait because she's in the army.

174
00:08:37.680 --> 00:08:39.440
So, I invited Angela.

175
00:08:39.820 --> 00:08:42.600
And he makes up some stupid reason that Michael believes.

176
00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:46.020
So, they all end up having beet wine and lots of beets.

177
00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:50.000
And this meal is generally disgusting, is what this document says.

178
00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.880
Eventually, Dwight introduces Michael to his dad.

179
00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:57.480
And his dad instantly dislikes Michael because Michael made a joke about the beets.

180
00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:01.340
In A Talking Head, Dwight's dad says, Michael is frivolous and stupid.

181
00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:05.200
And Dwight is very upset that his two father figures do not get along.

182
00:09:05.480 --> 00:09:15.160
So, this whole Thanksgiving sort of sets up tension between Dwight and Angela, Dwight and Michael, and Dwight and his family.

183
00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:16.800
So, that was that storyline.

184
00:09:17.560 --> 00:09:19.280
And Angela and Oscar.

185
00:09:19.760 --> 00:09:21.640
Yes, this ongoing lawsuit.

186
00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:26.720
But there was also a Karen, Jim, and Pam storyline for this episode.

187
00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.340
Karen asked Jim if he wants to go with her to her parents' place in Stanford.

188
00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:33.140
She said, it's totally low-key.

189
00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:34.120
They just watch football.

190
00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:34.800
No big deal.

191
00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:38.840
Jim says he thinks it might be too soon to meet her parents.

192
00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.180
And Karen says, I totally understand.

193
00:09:41.840 --> 00:09:47.320
Meanwhile, Pam is in charge of taking all the canned food from the Dunder Mifflin Food Drive to a homeless shelter.

194
00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.080
And she asked Jim if he wants to help her.

195
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:51.380
And Jim says yes.

196
00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:56.640
So, he says no to going to Karen's thing, but yes to helping Pam.

197
00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:57.480
Well, yeah.

198
00:09:58.000 --> 00:09:59.800
So, Pam and Jim head to the shelter.

199
00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:01.700
They hand out food and talk.

200
00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:03.440
And it's kind of like the old days.

201
00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:10.000
But then Jim heads home early because he's decided to go to Stanford the next day to be with Karen after all.

202
00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:14.060
And Pam realizes it's actually not like it used to be.

203
00:10:14.840 --> 00:10:17.780
And that was going to be that little Thanksgiving love triangle.

204
00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:19.460
So, there you have it.

205
00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:20.520
Look at that.

206
00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.600
All that stuff.

207
00:10:21.820 --> 00:10:22.580
All those ideas.

208
00:10:23.000 --> 00:10:24.180
How good were our writers?

209
00:10:24.400 --> 00:10:25.820
None of that even got made.

210
00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:26.500
I know.

211
00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.800
What a fun, fun pitch.

212
00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:34.840
And I wonder how many times they had to break out and work on a pitch and then it never even saw the light of day.

213
00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:42.540
I think a lot because clearly there was a whole storyline about this slap and this lawsuit that never came to fruition either.

214
00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.260
Well, that's all we got for this week.

215
00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:46.340
